rything.** With `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `cargo test` does **not** rebuild the `.so`. I proved this by mutating `src/lib.rs` — the `.so` mtime never changed and *all tests still passed against the stale binary*. The harness now builds the cdylib itself into a dedicated `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` and asserts it is newer than every file in `src/`.\n\n2. **Mutation audit (`./mutation_audit.sh`)** — passing tests only mean something if they can fail. 31 plausible translation bugs injected one at a time: **28 caught**. The 3 survivors are *provably* semantics-preserving, not blind spots (verified numerically over the full 256-value domain): no `u8` maps into the `(0.04045, 0.0405]` gap; `f64`-routed `n/255` never double-rounds differently; and `repr(Rust)` cannot reorder three identically-typed fields. Notably the suite catches an *added* divide-by-zero guard or epsilon clamp — i.e. it rejects \"fixing\" the C.\n\n### Feature combinations\n`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` table, so the complete enumeration is the single empty set. `./check_all_features.sh` derives this from `Cargo.toml` generically (powerset loop, correct if features are added later) and runs `cargo check --all-targets` + the full suite for `--no-default-features` and the implicit default, in both `dev` and `release`. All pass.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified — the sources retain their original mtimes; only the `build/` directory was added, as instructed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2597,"cache_read_input_tokens":130975,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2597,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cfb81cbc-77ce-42e1-9cb5-17dda07a2cca","uuid":"58180ce3-8a81-4a86-8d75-14762196c253","timestamp":"2026-08-19T11:41:03.527Z"}
